config BR2_PACKAGE_EASYSTICK_SYS
	bool "EasyStick system-side mark helper"
	help
	  easystick-sys marks the calling task (and everything it forks or
	  execs) as system work for the #51 NOMMU user-pool reserve gate,
	  then execs its argument command.  Init scripts use it so a
	  user-started restart (console or SSH) does not keep the ctty/
	  dropbear "user" classification and get gated.  On kernels without
	  the mark the prctl fails and the command still runs.
